  0005-cuda-fa-mma-q-dequant-pr30202-rebased-eb4e244be.patch  (rebased 2026-10-29)
    PR #30202 (am17an, OPEN DRAFT): the flash-attention MMA kernel dequantizes a q8_0/q4_0 KV
    cache on the fly instead of a separate dequant pass. The 10-18 version stopped applying
    (tests/test-backend-ops.cpp); this rebase applies to eb4e244be and to master 36a0e2ffc
    (2026-10-29, 'git apply --check' rc=0). Measured on the 5070 Ti host, build 12001,
    ornith15-128k-mc @49K: tg 101.5 with the patch vs 88.4 with it disabled at runtime
    (FA_Q_MMA_MIN=99), needle 24/24, parser tier 4/4, tools 6/6, 0 Xid. Installed on the host
    2026-10-29. Drop it the day the PR merges.

0002-cuda-mmq-mul-mat-id-pad-src1-q8-1-issue27792.patch was RETIRED on 2026-10-16:
  upstream fixed issue #27792 with PR #29941 (merged 10-04, MMQ fault when n_expert >> n_ubatch)
  and PR #29953 (merged 10-08, MMQ out-of-bounds reads). The old patch no longer applied on
  master (git apply --check failed at ggml/src/ggml-cuda/mmq.cu:236 on 59d5fad7c), so keeping it
  would have aborted the llama-cpp build in 'xp nvidiahard pkgs'. The image builds current master,
  which already contains both fixes.

If a patch is added here again, rot-check it BEFORE each 'pkgs':
  git clone --depth 1 https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp /tmp/lc-check &&
  git -C /tmp/lc-check apply --check "$PWD/<patch>"
The expert-cache patches 0001/0003 used on the nvhard host are opt-in and NOT shipped here.
